Without a search domain, the OS resolver sends bare hostnames (e.g., `web0`, `web_server_0`) as-is (i.e., as the FQDN `web0.`), which doesn't match the authoritative `local` zone on the DNS server. The server (with `recursion no`) returns REFUSED, and all server name lookups fail. IP-level connectivity is fully intact; this is purely a DNS client configuration fault.

